{
  "_comment": "Golden vectors for stay derivation (src/stay). Each is a list of fixes in stored order, the stay rows another writer has put in the table, and the 'derived' rows that must result. extractStays must return exactly `expect`; deriveStays must leave exactly those rows in the store, whether it sees the fixes in one run or stops and starts again from the store after each count in `restart_after`, and whether the visit rows are written before the fixes or after them. Integers and `closed` must match exactly; lat and lon within coordinate_tolerance_deg; radius_m within radius_tolerance_m. See contracts/README.md.",
  "stay_radius_m": 150,
  "stay_min_duration_sec": 900,
  "stay_merge_gap_sec": 1800,
  "coordinate_tolerance_deg": 1e-9,
  "radius_tolerance_m": 0.001,
  "vectors": [
    {
      "name": "a clean single stay",
      "why": "Four fixes at home over 45 minutes, a fix at the office on either side. The stay runs from the first home fix to the last. The home fixes are 0, +2e-4, -2e-4 and 0 degrees of latitude from home, so the centroid is home; the third is 3e-4 degrees (33.3585 m) from the centroid of the first two, which is the radius.",
      "samples": [
        { "ts_utc": 1791000000, "lat": 12.9816, "lon": 77.5946 },
        { "ts_utc": 1791000900, "lat": 12.9716, "lon": 77.5946 },
        { "ts_utc": 1791001800, "lat": 12.9718, "lon": 77.5946 },
